  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "After the reported 1947 crash of a flying object near Roswell, New Mexico, everything was said to have been flown out, including metal I-beams marked with hieroglyph-like writing and a number of plates. A physicist named John Brandenburg says he heard this at a conference called Reminiscences of Roswell, from surviving officers and from the daughters of the local sheriff. If true, it would mean the wreckage was not of human making."
